cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "Donghyunpa (동현파): an educational C. elegans touch-circuit laboratory controlled through the esoteric language Donghyun-lang"
type: software
version: "1.02"
date-released: "2026-10-26"
authors:
  - family-names: Kim
    given-names: Dong Hyun
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9883-0229"
    affiliation: "Inha University College of Medicine"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Raspberry-Kim/donghyun-lab2"
url: "https://raspberry-kim.github.io/donghyun-lab2/"
abstract: >-
  Donghyunpa is a browser-based, noncommercial educational laboratory in
  which a pixel-art boxer touches a cartoon nematode and the response is
  computed on the publicly released C. elegans connectome of 279 neurons
  (CoMuNeLab C. elegans Multiplex Connectome; electrical, chemical monadic
  and chemical polyadic layers, 3,108 layer-specific connections). All
  actions are specified only through the esoteric programming language
  Donghyun-lang. The activity model is a constrained teaching model, not a
  biological measurement. The MIT license applies only to the original
  application code, documentation and artwork; the connectivity database and
  its derivative are made available under the Open Database License (ODbL)
  1.0, individual contents under the Database Contents License (DbCL) 1.0,
  and the fonts under the SIL Open Font License. See LICENSE, CREDITS.md and
  PROVENANCE.md.
keywords:
  - neuroscience education
  - Caenorhabditis elegans
  - connectome
  - touch circuit
  - esoteric programming language
  - JavaScript
